    "Outline (Bevo Mill: the Dutch windmill and the stone restaurant joined to it, with its patio and the trees round it): the drawing is choppy, blotchy and muddled, and the windmill's sails are uneven. Redraw the whole complex crisp and clean in the map's flat illustration style: the windmill as a whitewashed tapered tower with a dark conical cap, small windows and a door, and four identical, evenly spaced lattice sails in a clean X, all four the same length and width, mounted on one hub at the centre of the cap; the restaurant as one clean stone building with steep dark roofs, a chimney, tidy windows and a string-lit patio with orange umbrellas; the trees round it whole with round crowns, trunks and shadows. Keep the complex at the same position, size and footprint; the paths and the parking lot keep their exact positions and join the ones outside the outline."
