   "fixes": [
    "Outline (the steel arches of the Eads Bridge above its deck, across all spans): the curved arch ribs and their supports are broken, tangled and random, different on every span. Redraw every span with one consistent, realistic steel arch structure. Each span is a pair of parallel steel arch ribs, one behind the other; each rib is one smooth, evenly curved arch made of two parallel curved chords joined by a regular zig-zag truss of evenly spaced diagonals; the two ribs are joined across the top by evenly spaced straight cross braces. Straight vertical hangers, evenly spaced and parallel, drop from the ribs to the deck railing, the same spacing on every span. A thin railing runs along the walkway just above the cream deck. All steel is dark slate blue with a lighter top edge; every member is straight or smoothly curved, with no broken, crossing, doubled or wandering lines. All spans are identical in structure, differing only by perspective. The stone piers, the cream deck below the outline, the two street lamps, the water, the far bank, the trees and the grain elevator stay exactly as they are."
   ]
