 "notes": {
  "road": "Joe (4x crop north-east of the Carondelet lake): clean up the road and make the striping consistent. The road faded to a pale smear between the two big trees (about x 940 to 1050), its width wandered, and the centre dashes were faint on the west and irregular on the east. roadbands redraws x 575 to 1285 as one band: top and bottom edges fitted from the clean columns (a 10 to 17 px run near a guide line), interpolated over the smear and smoothed; the surface flat road colour, trees in front of the road kept; centre dashes 6 px long every 16 px; brick, trunks and crowns in front of the road are kept (the fire station's tower rises over its south edge and is protected), pale ghost crowns and lawn smears on the road become road",
  "bevo": "Joe (4x crop): Bevo Mill is still a little choppy and the sails need cleaning. The complex goes to the model on a 256 px tile, so it is drawn at about five times the master's resolution and downsampled",
  "eads": "Joe (4x crop): all the curved support beams of the Eads Bridge are broken and random; the whole bridge needs one consistent structure for the arches and realistic vertical supports. The area follows the arches' upper outline (a running minimum over 13 columns, 6 px above) down to the top of the cream deck slab, which stays with the piers so the rider's deck is untouched; the two lamps are protected pixel-tight (post, arm, lantern), so the arch feet beside them are redrawn; the model's water is used throughout the area (keeping the base water also kept the old hangers' soft cyan edges as faint ghost lines). The illustration keeps its through-arches over the deck (the real bridge's arches run under the deck), as the approved composition has them"
 }
